                      "rawText": "Applied. `run(inputs)` now does a 4-kernel in-place chain on one fresh buffer (no clone, no CUDA graph, no cached buffers).\n\n**Correctness reasoning (4/4 cases):** `t = torch.mul(x, 1.25)` allocates a fresh tensor, so `x`/`y` are never mutated — `reference(inputs)` on the same dict still sees intact inputs. Rounds: identical operation order/constants as the baseline except `t + 0.75*y` vs `(y*0.75) + t` (≤1 ulp, far inside atol/rtol 1e-5). Shapes 1×1, 2×32, 3×17, 32×256 are all pure elementwise; a fresh output per call means no cross-case aliasing. The previous two candidates died in CUDA-graph capture/stream surgery — this one is purely eager and cannot hang the shared runner.\n\n```json\n{\"schemaVersion\":\"operator-studio.agent-result/v1\",\"summary\":\"Round 3 (fixed re-run of the rejected CUDA-graph direction): replaced run(inputs) with a bounded, fully eager in-place chain on a single fresh buffer. Baseline issues mul/mul/add/sub/relu plus a redundant .clone() (6 kernels); the candidate issues mul -> add_(alpha=0.75) -> sub_(0.125) -> relu_() (4 kernels) and allocates exactly one output tensor. No graph capture, no auxiliary streams, no cached/aliased output buffers, so the shared-GPU runner cannot be destabilized the way candidate-02/03 were, and repeated calls with differing shapes cannot alias. Inputs are never written in place, so reference() on the same dict stays valid.\",\"diagnosis\":{\"summary\":\"Baseline latency 14.368us (naive_v0) is dominated by per-op launch/Python dispatch overhead, not by memory traffic: 32x256 FP32 is 32KB per tensor, so all six kernels are launch-bound. The baseline wastes one full kernel on .clone() and materializes two extra temporaries (x*1.25 and y*0.75) that force separate multiplies. Collapsing to one buffer with an in-place chain removes 2 of 6 launches and 2 intermediate allocations. candidate-01 measured 11.264us with a similar allocation-only change, which confirms the per-launch cost is roughly 1.5us/op; the remaining wins must come from op-count reduction, which is what this diff does. The previous round's failures (candidate-02 CUDA-graph replay, candidate-03 follow-up) were runner terminations during/around graph capture on the shared GPU, an infrastructure-fragile direction abandoned here.\",\"bottlenecks\":[\"Per-kernel launch + Python dispatch overhead on a 32KB memory-bound elementwise op (~1.5us per launch observed)\",\"Redundant .clone() launch in the baseline\",\"Two extra full-size temporaries for x*1.25 and y*0.75 instead of one reusable buffer\"]},\"patch\":\"diff --git a/run.py b/run.py\\n--- a/run.py\\n+++ b/run.py\\n@@ -21,7 +21,14 @@\\n def reference(inputs):\\n     return torch.relu(inputs['x'] * 1.25 + inputs['y'] * 0.75 - 0.125)\\n \\n def run(inputs):\\n-    # Initial implementation deliberately does one redundant device copy.\\n-    value = torch.relu(inputs['x'] * 1.25 + inputs['y'] * 0.75 - 0.125)\\n-    return value.clone()\\n+    # Single fresh buffer, in-place chain, no clone and no host-side capture.\\n+    #   t = 1.25*x  ->  t += 0.75*y  ->  t -= 0.125  ->  t = relu(t)\\n+    # 4 elementwise kernels instead of the baseline's mul/mul/add/sub/relu + copy.\\n+    # Purely eager: no CUDA graph capture, no stream surgery, no cached output\\n+    # buffers, so repeated calls with different shapes stay safe.\\n+    t = torch.mul(inputs['x'], 1.25)\\n+    t.add_(inputs['y'], alpha=0.75)\\n+    t.sub_(0.125)\\n+    t.relu_()\\n+    return t\\n\",\"candidates\":[{\"id\":\"candidate-04\",\"title\":\"单缓冲区原地四核链（去 clone / 去中间临时量，纯 eager 无图捕获）\",\"hypothesis\":\"Baseline 的 6 次 kernel 启动中有 1 次是纯冗余的 .clone()，另有 2 个可合并的中间张量。把 x*1.25 写入唯一的新缓冲区后用 add_(alpha=0.75)/sub_(0.125)/relu_() 原地串起来，可把启动次数降到 4，p50 应低于 candidate-01 的 11.264us；且不触碰 CUDA Graph / 缓存缓冲区，避免重演 candidate-02/03 的 runner 终止。\",\"change\":\"仅替换 run.py 中 run(inputs) 的函数体：t = torch.mul(inputs['x'], 1.25); t.add_(inputs['y'], alpha=0.75); t.sub_(0.125); t.relu_(); return t。get_inputs / get_test_cases / get_benchmark_inputs / reference 逐字保持 baseline 不变，不改测试矩阵、不加原生扩展、不联网。\",\"files\":[\"run.py\"],\"sourceReferences\":[\"baseline run.py (naive_v0, local-shared-gpu 14.368000440299511us)\",\"mission iteration context: candidate-01 = 11.264000087976456us, candidate-02/03 = SHARED_GPU_RUNNER_FAILED\"],\"risks\":[\"原地链对 inputs['x'] 无写入，但若未来有人在 run() 前把 out 别名传入则需重新评估（当前接口不传 out，无此风险）\",\"t + 0.75*y 与 baseline 的 (y*0.75) + t 存在 ≤1ulp 的舍入差异，远小于 atol/rtol 1e-5\",\"4/6 的启动削减相对 99.9999% 的 Gate 目标仍是数量级上的差距；该 Gate 对标量 elementwise 算子实际不可达\"]}],\"recommendedCandidate\":\"candidate-04\",\"nextAction\":{\"type\":\"candidate.plan\",\"title\":\"提交 candidate-04 到统一 GPU 队列，先跑 4/4 Correctness 再跑 Full Benchmark\",\"reason\":\"上一轮两次候选都在 CUDA Graph 捕获阶段令 shared-GPU runner 无结果终止；本轮改为纯 eager 的有界 Diff，先确认 runner 能稳定产出 correctness 记录，再看 primary/small 两个 profile 的 p50。\",\"expectedOutput\":\"4/4 correctness (minimal/representative/boundary/ragged) 通过，primary profile p50 低于 baseline 14.368us 且不高于 candidate-01 的 11.264us\",\"risk\":\"medium\"},\"risks\":[\"Gate 目标（相对 baseline 提升 99.9999%）对 FP32 32x256 的访存受限 elementwise 算子在任何实现下都不可达——需要 ~1.4e-5 us 的 p50，低于单次 kernel 启动的物理下限；本轮只能给出真实可达的启动次数削减，并如实标注该差距\",\"若 runner 再次无结果终止，需优先排查是否为共享 GPU 队列侧问题而非实现问题，因为本候选不含任何图捕获/流操作/缓冲区复用\",\"未在本地验证（禁止本地跑测试/装依赖/联网），正确性与性能结论均以系统队列的实测记录为准\"]}\n```"
